        "name": "USN-5811-2",
        "description": "USN-5811-1 fixed a vulnerability in Sudo. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 16.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   Matthieu Barjole and Victor Cutillas discovered that Sudo incorrectly  handled user-specified editors when using the sudoedit command. A local  attacker that has permission to use the sudoedit command could possibly use  this issue to edit arbitrary files. (CVE-2023-22809)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2023-22809"
        ]
